<section id="guardrails">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guardrails</p>
    <h2>Agents move fast. Mistakes stay small.</h2>
    <p>Risk reduction, not a security boundary. Claude Code focus sessions on macOS and Linux run open with a short block list. Lanes that read outside input run closed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ledger diagram reveal" role="table" aria-label="What focus sessions and outside input lanes can and cannot do">
    <div class="ledger-row ledger-head" role="row">
      <span role="columnheader"></span>
      <span role="columnheader" class="yes"><span class="column-name">Your focus sessions</span><span class="posture">Open, blocks a list</span></span>
      <span role="columnheader" class="no"><span class="column-name">Outside input lanes</span><span class="posture">Closed, allows a list</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger-row" role="row">
      <span class="aspect" role="rowheader">Writes</span>
      <span role="cell" class="yes" data-level="Your focus sessions"><span class="verdict">Anywhere</span><span class="detail">Except credentials, Glimmervoid's state, <code>blockedPaths</code></span></span>
      <span role="cell" class="no" data-level="Outside input lanes"><span class="verdict">Own folder only</span><span class="detail">Not even git hooks</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger-row" role="row">
      <span class="aspect" role="rowheader">Reads</span>
      <span role="cell" class="yes" data-level="Your focus sessions"><span class="verdict">All but credentials and state</span><span class="detail">And <code>unreadablePaths</code></span></span>
      <span role="cell" class="no" data-level="Outside input lanes"><span class="verdict">No credentials, no state</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger-row" role="row">
      <span class="aspect" role="rowheader">Network</span>
      <span role="cell" class="yes" data-level="Your focus sessions"><span class="verdict">Open</span></span>
      <span role="cell" class="no" data-level="Outside input lanes"><span class="verdict">Allowlist for reviews</span><span class="detail">Open for lanes that push a fix</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger-row" role="row">
      <span class="aspect" role="rowheader">Tools</span>
      <span role="cell" class="yes" data-level="Your focus sessions"><span class="verdict">Everything</span></span>
      <span role="cell" class="no" data-level="Outside input lanes"><span class="verdict">Own terminal only</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="ledger-row" role="row">
      <span class="aspect" role="rowheader">Opt out</span>
      <span role="cell" class="yes" data-level="Your focus sessions"><span class="verdict">Per project</span></span>
      <span role="cell" class="no" data-level="Outside input lanes"><span class="verdict">Never</span></span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="built-on reveal">Built on <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/sandbox-runtime">Anthropic's sandbox-runtime</a> (Seatbelt on macOS, bubblewrap on Linux) and <a href="https://ccsafetynet.com">CC Safety Net</a>.</p>
  <div class="yolo reveal">
    <div class="yolo-copy">
      <h3>Sane YOLO</h3>
      <p>Skip prompts without betting the repo. Claude Code, Codex and Grok commands are checked before they run; <code>git reset --hard</code>, <code>git push --force</code> and unverifiable <code>rm -rf</code> are refused. On by default.</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="yolo-term" aria-label="A blocked command in a session"><span class="prompt">$</span> rm -rf "$BUILD_DIR"
<span class="blocked">BLOCKED by CC Safety Net</span>

Reason: rm -rf target contains shell variables
that cannot be verified safely.</pre>
  </div>
</section>

